  "inclusive_survival_formula_supported": false,
  "latest_open_gate": "PrimeDivisibilityClassIsOneOverPNotOneMinusOneOverP AND ExactLPFBucketCountIsLegendrePhiNotInclusiveSurvivalProduct AND UnsignedLPFBucketCountStillParityBlind AND VonMangoldtLiftRequiresGlobalDivisorSignedPayloadNotLPFLocalCount",
  "phi_lpf_parity_barrier_globally_broken": false,
  "plain_conclusion": "The revised formula fixes the survival factors for primes q<p, but it treats p itself as another survival prime. LPF(n)=p instead requires divisibility by p. Thus the p-factor is 1/p, not 1-1/p. The exact identity remains a Legendre-Phi rough-number count and stays parity-blind without a signed divisor payload.",
  "reason_user_formula_fails": "For q<p the LPF bucket survives nonzero classes. For p itself the bucket requires the zero class n=0 mod p, whose density is 1/p, not the nonzero-class density 1-1/p.",
